# Generic Device Plugin — required for FUSE-without-privileged
#
# The agent-computer Pod's `/workspace` is a FUSE mount (cumora-fuse
# Go binary, see agent-fuse/main.go). FUSE mount needs:
#   1. CAP_SYS_ADMIN
#   2. Access to /dev/fuse
#
# CAP_SYS_ADMIN we can grant directly in the Pod's securityContext.
# /dev/fuse is gated by containerd's device cgroup whitelist — even
# with the cap, opening /dev/fuse returns EPERM unless something
# adds it to the allowlist. `privileged: true` does that (along with
# everything else); a *device plugin* does it surgically.
#
# We use squat/generic-device-plugin. Install:
#
#   kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/squat/generic-device-plugin/main/manifests/generic-device-plugin.yaml
#
# Prod override: after installing the upstream DaemonSet, patch the
# advertised /dev/fuse count to 800 slots per node:
#
#   kubectl patch daemonset generic-device-plugin -n kube-system --type=json \
#     -p='[{"op":"replace","path":"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args/5","value":"name: fuse\ngroups:\n  - count: 800\n    paths:\n      - path: /dev/fuse\n"}]'
#
# Confirms with:
#   kubectl describe node <node-name> | grep devic.es/fuse
#   # Should show `devic.es/fuse: 800` under Allocatable.
#
# The agent Pod manifest (orchestrator.ts) requests this resource
# via `resources.limits["devic.es/fuse"]: 1` and adds CAP_SYS_ADMIN.
# No `privileged: true`. Runtime admission still applies the lower
# app-level AGENT_POD_ADMISSION_MAX cap (default 40), so this device
# count is not the effective production pod ceiling.
#
# DaemonSet lands in the `kube-system` namespace by default. It
# advertises /dev/fuse (800 slots per node in prod) plus a handful of other generic devices
# (audio, tun, kvm) which we don't use but don't hurt.
#
# If the cluster runs without this plugin installed, agent Pods
# will fail to schedule with:
#   0/1 nodes are available: 1 Insufficient devic.es/fuse.
